  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mi>OH</mi><mo>⇒</mo></math> Intermolecular <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math>-Bonding</p><p>The hydrogen bonding which takes place within a molecule itself is called intramolecular hydrogen bonding.</p><p>It takes place in compounds containing two groups such that one group contains a hydrogen atom linked to an electronegative atom and the other group contains a highly electronegative atom linked to another electronegative atom of the other group.</p><p>The bond is formed between the hydrogen atoms of one group with the more electronegative atom of the other group.</p><p>So the answer is:</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0062_f6b2c0bbf063.png\" style=\"width: 450px; height: 182px;\"/></p>"
